.TH CYAML_CLONE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cyaml_clone \- produce a deep independent copy of a DOM subtree
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cyaml.h>

cyaml cyaml_clone(cyaml node);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Recursively copy node and all of its descendants.  The clone uses the
same allocator as the source tree.  Mutating the clone does not affect
the original and vice versa.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
node  Root of the subtree to copy.  NULL is accepted and returns NULL.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Root of the new tree (caller owns it), or NULL on allocation failure.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_destroy (3)
